awesome smelling baked goods, but I mostly stuck with coffee and a bagel to go. overall its a good place to visit in the morning if you're at one of the hotels, and is much better than any of the hotel coffee places"},{"business_id":"4FDOh7BAb0pgLuD8rjl3bg","review_id":"-K4S1nGLcqNUQtTThWC0vA","date":"2010-11-25T05:14:45","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9190194010734558,"text_excerpt":"I heard about this cute and quaint place through the grapevine at my workplace, and happened to come across it on Yelp! I rolled in on a humid Monday morning, and decided to go for an iced coffee (coffee ice cubes!). The ridin-solo barista was friendly and quick- all the while he maintained conversation with customers while steaming milk and pulling shots, etc. Also, I noticed the yummy desserts and pastries for an awfully great price! Next time I stop by, I'll make sure to order a latte/cappuccino and hopefully I score some foam art :) Another plus: wifi!"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
